@page "/sheet"
@implements IDisposable
@using System.Globalization
@* global::, because this project's namespace nests inside ExGrid (the CS0426 trap in AGENTS.md),
   and because inside ExSheet.Components the name ExSheet is the component, not the namespace. *@
@using global::ExSheet
@using global::ExSheet.Components
@using global::ExSheet.Engine
@using global::ExGrid.Chrome
@using global::ExGrid.MudBlazor

@* ?chrome=mud runs the Sheet with ExGrid.MudBlazor's Chrome instead of the built-in one, so the
   browser tests of the Formula Bar, the completion list and the coloured text run under both
   Chromes (DC-17, ADR-0030; DemoChrome). Unlike /features, which changes the Chrome alone, the
   Sheet stands on the Wrapper's paper with its stylesheet: the Chrome's fields meet the coloured
   text's contract (no padding, no ground, filling the core's box) only through that stylesheet,
   and the Chrome used alone is not supported where References are coloured (ADR-0057, "The
   Wrapper's shape is required…"; ADR-0030). Its Chrome is ExSheet.MudBlazor's, which is the
   Wrapper's in every seam of the grid and draws Format Cells as a MudDialog (ADR-0071). *@
@* ?scheme=dark shows the page in the dark scheme, where the Sheet's Paper stays white and its frame
   darkens (ADR-0071). ?case= opens one of the eleventh Windows run's set-ups instead of the page's own
   Sheet (SheetCases), for Part C to put beside Excel's screenshots. *@
<DemoChromeAssets Name="@ChromeName" Paper="true" Sheet="true" Dark="Dark" />

<DemoNav />

<h1>Sheet — ExSheet drawn by ExGrid</h1>

<p>
    ExSheet holds a Sheet of Entries and computes their Values; one ExGrid paints it, as that grid's
    Consumer (ADR-0046). Type into a cell, press F2 on a Formula to edit it, read the Entry in the
    Formula Bar, type an address such as <code>D200</code> into the Name Box, and use Ctrl+arrow to
    jump to the end of a block. The status line counts the cells of the Sheet Document the page
    receives after every change (ADR-0048).
</p>

<p>
    The grid on the right shows this page's positions, and the Sheet reads the same data as the
    Linked Table <code>Positions</code> (ADR-0049): by key in B12, by column in B11. Its key column is
    <code>Id</code>, so a snapshot in which an Id repeats would be refused and its readers would wait
    again. The page pushes its first snapshot a moment after the Sheet opens, so those cells show <code>#GETTING_DATA</code>
    until it lands; <i>Revalue</i> changes the data both show, and only the Formulas reading the
    table recalculate. Type <code>=SUM(Po</code> into a cell to see the table offered, and finish it as
    <code>=SUM(Positions[PV])</code>: while the Formula is edited, the PV column of the grid on the right
    is outlined in the colour its Reference wears (ADR-0057). The Sheet tells which columns it reads,
    and the Pointing Scope the page put the Sheet and that grid in, which knows that the grid shows the
    table, outlines them there (ADR-0058). Click a header of the grid on the right to sort it.
</p>

<div class="demo-toolbar">
    <button id="sheet-undo" disabled="@_editing" @onclick="UndoAsync">Undo</button>
    <button id="sheet-redo" disabled="@_editing" @onclick="RedoAsync">Redo</button>
    <button id="sheet-money" disabled="@_editing" @onclick="FormatMoneyAsync">Format selection as #,##0.00</button>
    <button id="sheet-format-cells" disabled="@_editing" @onclick="FormatCellsAsync">Format Cells…</button>
    <button id="sheet-insert-row" disabled="@_editing" @onclick="InsertRowAsync">Insert a row above row 2</button>
    <button id="sheet-revalue" @onclick="RevalueAsync">Revalue the positions by +1%</button>
</div>

<p class="demo-status">
    <span id="sheet-status">@_status</span>
</p>

@* ?box=window gives the Sheet a box that follows the window's height (ViewportSize.Stretch), so a
   popover's room changes with the window: the browser tests shrink it under Format Cells
   (DC-60, ADR-0040). *@
<div class="demo-side-by-side" style="@(InWindowBox ? "height: calc(100vh - 360px); min-height: 0" : null)">
    @if (DemoChrome.IsMud(ChromeName))
    {
        <MudExGridPaper>@Sheet</MudExGridPaper>
    }
    else
    {
        @Sheet
    }
    <div id="sheet-positions">
        <ExGrid TRow="Position" Source="_positionsShown" Columns="PositionColumns" RowHeight="28"
                ViewportHeight="420" ViewportWidth="330" PointedAt="_positionsPointedAt" />
    </div>
</div>

@* Why a press on the positions grid wrote nothing into the Formula, as the Sheet tells the page
   (ADR-0058). Below the grids, for the reason the paragraph below gives. *@
<p class="demo-status">
    <span id="sheet-pointing">@_pointingStatus</span>
</p>

@* Below the Sheet, not above it: the page's tests press cells by where the grid stands in a
   720 px window, and text above the grid moves every row down. *@
<p class="demo-status">
    Focus cell: <span id="sheet-focus-font">@_focusFont</span>,
    <span id="sheet-focus-number-format">@_focusNumberFormat</span>
</p>

<p>
    Excel's formatting keys work on the Selection, each as one step Ctrl+Z undoes (ADR-0071): Ctrl+B,
    Ctrl+I, Ctrl+U and Ctrl+5 (or Ctrl+2 to Ctrl+4) toggle bold, italic, underline and
    strikethrough from the Focus cell's state, and Ctrl+Shift with <code>~ ! @@ # $ % ^</code> applies
    General, <code>#,##0.00</code>, a time, a date, the currency, a percentage and scientific; with
    <code>&amp;</code> an outline, and with <code>_</code> no borders. The line above reads the
    Focus cell's Cell Format back. While a cell is being edited the keys change nothing, and the
    Sheet says why.
</p>

<p>
    The Sheet and the positions grid are in one Pointing Scope (ADR-0058). While a Formula is typed,
    wherever a Reference can go — after <code>=</code>, an operator, <code>(</code> or <code>,</code>
    — a press on a positions cell writes what reads it by its key,
    <code>XLOOKUP("R-4471", Positions[Id], Positions[PV])</code>, and a press on a column's header
    writes <code>Positions[PV]</code>. The positions grid keeps neither the keyboard nor a Selection for
    it: the pressed cell or column is dashed until something is typed after what the press wrote, and
    the dashes stay on that position's row wherever a sort puts it. A press that stands for more than
    one cell writes nothing, and the line above says why.
</p>

<p>
    While a cell is being edited, the commands that change the Sheet are greyed out, as Excel greys
    out its ribbon: ExSheet refuses them until the edit is committed or cancelled, so a row inserted
    above the cell cannot carry the typing into another row (ADR-0048). <i>Revalue</i> stays: a
    Linked Table's snapshot is data arriving, not a command (ADR-0049).
</p>

@code {
    /// <summary>Which Chrome the Sheet runs with (<see cref="DemoChrome"/>).</summary>
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "chrome")]
    public string? ChromeName { get; set; }

    /// <summary><c>window</c> sizes the Sheet's height by the window's rather than declaring it.</summary>
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "box")]
    public string? Box { get; set; }

    private bool InWindowBox => Box == "window";

    /// <summary><c>dark</c> shows the page in the dark scheme (<see cref="DemoChrome.IsDark"/>).</summary>
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "scheme")]
    public string? Scheme { get; set; }

    /// <summary>One of the eleventh Windows run's cases (<see cref="SheetCases"/>), opened in place of the page's own Sheet.</summary>
    [SupplyParameterFromQuery(Name = "case")]
    public string? Case { get; set; }

    private bool Dark => DemoChrome.IsDark(Scheme);

    // The page's own Sheet pins column A; a run's case does not, as Excel's workbook in the run had
    // no frozen panes, so what Part C puts beside Excel's picture is drawn as Excel drew it.
    private int PinnedColumns => Case is null ? 1 : 0;

    private IGridChrome? _chrome;

    // The Sheet, on the Wrapper's paper under ExGrid.MudBlazor's Chrome and bare under the core's.
    private RenderFragment Sheet => @<ExSheet @ref="_sheet" @bind-Document="_document" @bind-Document:after="Count" Culture="Culture" PinnedColumnCount="@PinnedColumns" Chrome="_chrome"
                                              EditingChanged="_editingChanged" ViewportHeight="@(InWindowBox ? ViewportSize.Stretch : 420)" ViewportWidth="720"
                                              SelectionChanged="_selectionChanged" OnFormatKeyRefused="_formatKeyRefused"
                                              PointingScope="_scope" OnPointingRefused="ShowPointingRefusal" />;

    protected override void OnParametersSet() => _chrome = DemoChrome.ForSheet(ChromeName);

    private static readonly CultureInfo Culture = CultureInfo.GetCultureInfo("en-US");

    private const string Table = "Positions";
    private static readonly string[] TableColumns = ["Id", "Book", "PV"];
    // A row is read by its Id, and no Id appears twice in a snapshot (ADR-0049, 2026-09-30).
    private const string TableKey = "Id";

    // The page's own data: what the positions grid shows and what the Sheet reads, from one
    // source (ADR-0049's first rule: ExSheet never reads the grid).
    private sealed record Position(string Id, string Book, double PV);

    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<GridColumn<Position>> PositionColumns =
    [
        new("Id", ColumnType.Text, p => p.Id, width: new ColumnWidthSpec(ColumnWidth.Fixed(90))),
        new("Book", ColumnType.Text, p => p.Book, width: new ColumnWidthSpec(ColumnWidth.Fixed(90))),
        new("PV", ColumnType.Number, p => p.PV, width: new ColumnWidthSpec(ColumnWidth.Fixed(120)),
            format: v => ((double)v).ToString("N2", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)),
    ];

    private readonly CancellationTokenSource _closing = new();
    private static readonly Position[] OpeningPositions =
    [
        new("R-1102", "Rates", 1_250),
        new("R-2210", "Rates", -420.5),
        new("R-4471", "FX", 318.25),
        new("R-5093", "Credit", 97.4),
        new("R-6120", "FX", -55.75),
    ];
    private Position[] _positions = OpeningPositions;
    // The positions as the grid on the right shows them, sorted as its headers ask; the Sheet reads
    // the table by key, whatever order the grid shows (ADR-0049's second rule).
    private readonly InMemoryGridSource<Position> _positionsShown = GridSource.From(OpeningPositions);

    private ExSheet? _sheet;
    private SheetDocument? _document;
    // The Sheet and the positions grid, pointed at while the Sheet points (ADR-0058). The grid is
    // registered with the table it shows and how its rows are the table's rows: its columns are
    // named as the table's are declared, so no column needs an entry. The Scope also outlines there
    // the columns of the table the Formula being edited reads (ADR-0057): only the page knows which
    // grid shows the table (ADR-0049's first rule, ADR-0018), and it says so once, here.
    private readonly PointingScope _scope = new();
    private GridPointedAt<Position>? _positionsPointedAt;
    // Why the last press on the positions grid wrote nothing, until the edit opens or ends.
    private string _pointingStatus = "";
    private string _status = "";
    // Whether an edit is open in the Sheet, as ExSheet raises it: the toolbar's commands are
    // greyed out while it is (ADR-0048).
    private bool _editing;
    private EventCallback<bool> _editingChanged;
    // The Focus cell's Cell Format, read back from the Sheet whenever the Selection or the Sheet
    // changes (ADR-0071's CellFormatAt), and a formatting key the Sheet refused, said in the status
    // line as the page says a refused command (ADR-0071, SH-43).
    private EventCallback<GridSelection> _selectionChanged;
    private EventCallback<SheetRefusal> _formatKeyRefused;
    private GridSelection _selection = GridSelection.Empty;
    private string _focusFont = "";
    private string _focusNumberFormat = "";

    // A few values, Formulas over them, and a date: the tracer's A1 + B1 and a little more.
    private static SheetDocument Opening()
    {
        var sheet = new Sheet(Culture);
        (string Address, string Typed)[] cells =
        [
            ("A1", "Item"), ("B1", "Qty"), ("C1", "Price"), ("D1", "Amount"),
            ("A2", "Apples"), ("B2", "12"), ("C2", "0.5"), ("D2", "=B2*C2"),
            ("A3", "Pears"), ("B3", "7"), ("C3", "0.75"), ("D3", "=B3*C3"),
            ("A4", "Plums"), ("B4", "20"), ("C4", "0.2"), ("D4", "=B4*C4"),
            ("A5", "Total"), ("B5", "=SUM(B2:B4)"), ("D5", "=SUM(D2:D4)"),
            ("A7", "As of"), ("B7", "9/26/2026"),
            ("A8", "Due"), ("B8", "=B7+30"),
            ("A10", "Positions"),
            ("A11", "Total PV"), ("B11", $"=SUM({Table}[PV])"),
            ("A12", "PV of R-4471"), ("B12", $"=XLOOKUP(\"R-4471\", {Table}[Id], {Table}[PV])"),
            ("A13", "Count"), ("B13", $"=COUNTA({Table}[Id])"),
        ];
        // The declaration travels in the Sheet Document; the rows never do (ADR-0049).
        sheet.DeclareLinkedTable(Table, TableColumns, TableKey);
        foreach (var (address, typed) in cells) sheet.Enter(CellAddress.Parse(address), typed);
        return sheet.ToDocument();
    }

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        _document = SheetCases.Document(Case, Culture) ?? Opening();
        _positionsPointedAt = _scope.RegisterGrid<Position>(Table, TableRow);
        // Held in a field: a method group would be a new delegate on every render (AGENTS.md,
        // the Blazor traps).
        _editingChanged = EventCallback.Factory.Create<bool>(this, OnEditingChanged);
        _selectionChanged = EventCallback.Factory.Create<GridSelection>(this, OnSelectionChanged);
        _formatKeyRefused = EventCallback.Factory.Create<SheetRefusal>(this, refusal => _status = refusal.Message);
        Count();
    }

    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (!firstRender || _sheet is null) return;
        // Declaring what the document already declares changes nothing; a page that opens a
        // document without it declares it here.
        await _sheet.DeclareLinkedTableAsync(Table, TableColumns, TableKey);
        try
        {
            // Long enough to see #GETTING_DATA: the data is "on its way".
            await Task.Delay(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(1.5), _closing.Token);
        }
        catch (OperationCanceledException)
        {
            return;
        }
        await PushAsync();
    }

    private async Task RevalueAsync()
    {
        Position[] revalued = [.. _positions.Select(p => p with { PV = Math.Round(p.PV * 1.01, 2) })];
        // Each position is a new instance, where the grid shows it in the order it is sorted.
        for (var i = 0; i < revalued.Length; i++) _positionsShown.ReplaceRow(_positions[i], revalued[i]);
        _positions = revalued;
        await PushAsync();
    }

    private Task PushAsync() =>
        _sheet is null
            ? Task.CompletedTask
            : _sheet.PushLinkedTableAsync(Table, _positions.Select(TableRow));

    // A position as the table's row, in the declared column order: what the page pushes, and what
    // the Scope reads a pressed row's key from.
    private static IReadOnlyList<Value?> TableRow(Position p) => [Value.FromText(p.Id), Value.FromText(p.Book), Value.FromNumber(p.PV)];

    private void ShowPointingRefusal(PointingRefusal refusal) => _pointingStatus = refusal.Message;

    public void Dispose()
    {
        _closing.Cancel();
        _closing.Dispose();
    }

    private void OnEditingChanged(bool open)
    {
        _editing = open;
        _pointingStatus = "";
    }

    private Task UndoAsync() => CommandAsync(sheet => sheet.UndoAsync());

    private Task RedoAsync() => CommandAsync(sheet => sheet.RedoAsync());

    private Task FormatMoneyAsync() => CommandAsync(sheet => sheet.SetNumberFormatAsync(NumberFormat.Parse("#,##0.00")));

    private Task InsertRowAsync() => CommandAsync(sheet => sheet.DoAsync(SheetEdit.InsertRows(1)));

    // The Consumer's own button for Format Cells (ADR-0071), beside the Context Menu's command.
    private Task FormatCellsAsync() => CommandAsync(sheet => sheet.OpenFormatCellsAsync());

    // A command ExSheet refuses changes nothing and says why (ADR-0048): an insertion that would
    // push an Entry off the Sheet, or any command while an edit is open. The buttons are greyed
    // out then, but a press can still land before the render that greys them does.
    private async Task CommandAsync(Func<ExSheet, Task> command)
    {
        if (_sheet is null) return;
        try
        {
            await command(_sheet);
            Count();
        }
        catch (SheetRefusedException refused)
        {
            _status = refused.Message;
        }
    }

    private void Count()
    {
        _status = $"{_document?.Cells.Count ?? 0} cells in the Sheet Document.";
        ReadFocus();
    }

    private void OnSelectionChanged(GridSelection selection)
    {
        _selection = selection;
        ReadFocus();
    }

    private void ReadFocus()
    {
        if (_sheet is null || _selection.IsEmpty)
        {
            _focusFont = _focusNumberFormat = "";
            return;
        }
        var format = _sheet.CellFormatAt(new CellAddress(_selection.Focus.Row, _selection.Focus.Column));
        string[] emphases =
        [
            .. format.Font.Bold ? ["bold"] : Array.Empty<string>(),
            .. format.Font.Italic ? ["italic"] : Array.Empty<string>(),
            .. format.Font.Underline ? ["underline"] : Array.Empty<string>(),
            .. format.Font.Strikethrough ? ["strikethrough"] : Array.Empty<string>(),
        ];
        _focusFont = emphases.Length == 0 ? "regular" : string.Join(" ", emphases);
        _focusNumberFormat = format.NumberFormat.Code;
    }
}
